# {{ product_name }}

Thin Tauri 2 shell for a local Docker Compose stack. The window loads the URL from `shell.toml` after Compose starts. Business logic stays in the container images.

See [docs/reusable-compose-shell.md](docs/reusable-compose-shell.md) and [docs/tauri-docker-compose-thin-shell.md](docs/tauri-docker-compose-thin-shell.md).

## Run

`make init` installs the Rust toolchain (at least the `rust-version` in `src-tauri/Cargo.toml`), the Tauri 2 CLI, and the system WebView libraries. It does not install Docker Desktop. When `docker info` succeeds, development keeps using Docker. When Docker Desktop is installed and the daemon is stopped, init asks you to start it. When no Docker engine is available, init installs Podman and a Compose provider (2.20 or newer) and writes `podman` to `.container-runtime`. `make dev` and the `compose-*` targets export that choice as `CONTAINER_RUNTIME`.

On Windows, run `make` from Git Bash or MSYS2. `make init` uses winget for Visual Studio Build Tools, WebView2, Rust, and Podman. Podman needs WSL. If WSL is missing, init prints `wsl --install --no-distribution` for an administrator PowerShell and does not reboot the machine.

Release builds do not use Docker. On Windows, `make release` downloads the pinned Podman MSI and Compose provider, then the installer quietly installs Podman for the current user. The first launch still needs WSL: if it is missing, the app asks you to run `wsl --install --no-distribution` from an administrator PowerShell and restart.

```text
make init
make help
make test
make stack-check
make dev
make fetch-runtime
make release
```

`make dev` runs `cargo tauri dev --no-dev-server-wait`. That flag is required. The Tauri CLI would otherwise wait for port {{ ui_port }} before the shell is able to start Compose.

## Stack contract

Each stack is a directory with:

- `shell.toml` — product name, Compose project name, health URL, secret keys
- `docker-compose.yml` — services, ports, volumes, healthchecks
- `.env.example` — committed defaults; `.env` is gitignored and created on first run

The root stack starts `nginx:alpine` on `http://127.0.0.1:{{ ui_port }}`.
