Set `STACK_DIR` to run another stack during development. Unset `STACK_DIR` uses the repo root in debug builds. Release builds ignore `STACK_DIR` and engine path overrides, copy the bundled root stack into app data, and keep `.env` there.

`UI_HEALTH_URL` and `UI_WAIT_SECS` in the process environment override `.env` and `shell.toml`.

A boot window stays up while the engine starts, images pull, Compose healthchecks pass, and the UI health URL responds. Closing the app runs `compose down` without `-v`, so named volumes stay. It does not stop the Podman machine.

## Expected result today

With Docker running, `make dev` starts the nginx stack and opens the window. With Docker stopped, the dialog says Docker is not running. A Windows release build looks for Podman instead, and shows how to install WSL when that feature is missing.

## Updates

This app was generated with Copier. From this directory, `copier update` pulls engine fixes. That update leaves `docker-compose.yml`, `.env.example`, and `src-tauri/icons/` in place when those files already exist. `.container-runtime` is written by `make init` on this machine and is not part of the template.

Changing `identifier` in `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` after the first shipped installer publishes a different app.
